# News & Economic Calendar Filter Implementation

This plan implements the **News and Macro Filter** feature specified in the v1.0 blueprint (Section 5), which is currently stubbed out in [news.py](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/news.py). This is a critical risk management feature that blocks trades around high-impact economic events and integrates sentiment analysis.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Source Decision Required**
> 
> This implementation requires an economic calendar data source. Options:
> 
> 1. **CSV-based (Recommended for v1.0)**: Simple CSV file with columns: `timestamp`, `currency`, `impact`, `event_name`. You would manually maintain or download this file.
> 2. **API-based**: Integrate with services like ForexFactory, Investing.com, or Trading Economics (requires API key and internet connection).
> 
> The plan below uses **Option 1 (CSV)** for consistency with the existing offline-first architecture. If you prefer API integration, please specify which service.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking Change to StrategyEngine**
> 
> The `StrategyEngine.generate_signals()` method will be modified to accept an optional [NewsEngine](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/news.py#1-4) parameter. Existing code that directly instantiates [StrategyEngine](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py#40-132) will continue to work (news filter is optional), but the API server and backtest scripts will be updated to use the news filter.

## Proposed Changes

### Core News Filter Module

#### [MODIFY] [news.py](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/news.py)

Implement the [NewsEngine](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/news.py#1-4) class with:

- **Economic Calendar Loading**: Read events from CSV file with columns: `timestamp`, `currency`, `impact` (low/medium/high), `event_name`
- **Event Blocking Logic**: Check if current time is within blocking window (45 min before to 30 min after high-impact events)
- **Sentiment Analysis**: Simple keyword-based sentiment scoring for news headlines (returns score between -1.0 and +1.0)
- **Instrument Filtering**: Map currencies to instruments (e.g., "USD" affects EURUSD, GBPUSD, XAUUSD, etc.)

**Key Methods**:
- `is_blocked(instrument: str, timestamp: pd.Timestamp) -> bool`: Check if trading is blocked
- `get_sentiment_score(instrument: str, timestamp: pd.Timestamp) -> float`: Get sentiment score
- `should_reduce_risk(instrument: str, direction: str, timestamp: pd.Timestamp) -> bool`: Check if sentiment opposes trade direction

