### Strategy Engine Integration

#### [MODIFY] [strategy.py](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py)

Update [StrategyEngine](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py#40-132) to accept optional [NewsEngine](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/news.py#1-4):

- Add `news_engine: Optional[NewsEngine]` parameter to [__init__](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py#52-56)
- In [generate_signals()](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py#71-132), after generating candidate signals:
  1. Check `news_engine.is_blocked()` - skip signal if blocked
  2. Check `news_engine.should_reduce_risk()` - skip or reduce risk if sentiment opposes
- Add `news_blocked: bool` and `sentiment_score: float` fields to [Signal](file:///c:/Users/user/OneDrive/Documents/App-Web%20Dev/trx/src/v1_0/core/strategy.py#20-31) dataclass for transparency

